The interface has inconsistent peach/coral accents and black primary CTA buttons. Correct this globally.

- Use the existing muted purple brand accent, approximately `#7463A6`, with a pale purple tint around `#F1EEF8`.
- Replace remaining peach, coral, and reddish-orange primary accents with the muted purple brand colour.
- Replace black primary CTA buttons with consistent purple primary buttons.
- Standardise button height, radius, padding, typography, hover, focus, disabled, and loading states.
- Secondary actions should use appropriate neutral or outlined styling, not compete with the primary action.
- Do not apply purple indiscriminately to every icon or every status. Status colours must remain meaningful.
- Do not introduce gradients, glow effects, glassmorphism, neon colours, or unnecessary decorative elements.

### Universal KPI card rules

Apply the same KPI card structure and dimensions throughout the application.

- Preserve the existing Overview KPI card height as the standard reference.
- Keep the off-white outer shell, white inner card, subtle shadow, and balanced spacing.
- Use the existing Outfit font.
- Keep the KPI title, individual icon, and main figure.
- Remove the fourth component: the supporting or descriptive text beneath the main figure.
- **Removing supporting text must never reduce the card height.** Maintain the Overview KPI card height, inner-card position, and consistent spacing.
- Do not add new borders or decorative icon-background squares.
- Keep icons appropriately sized and individually coloured where appropriate.

This applies to Laundry Logger, Laundry Storage, Beverages, Food Inventory, Stock Keeper, Expenses, Finance Reports, and any other KPI cards in this batch unless a section explicitly says to retain or remove the entire KPI group.

